%description:

Tcp.pathMtu:route -- the search ends at the route MTU.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "with mtuProbing: the MTU of the route, the largest MTU that the search can
give the connection (Linux dst_mtu()); 0 = the MTU of the negotiated MSS".

The classes: negotiated (0, the default: the MTU of the MSS of the handshake) and route (a
route MTU below it). The code: TcpConnection::initMtuProbing() takes the value as the route
MTU, and TcpConnection::getMtuProbeBytes() keeps the probes at or below it. This test separates "route" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, with mtuProbing 2 (precondition); host1 sends 1000000 bytes to host2; the path carries 1500 bytes, and the MSS of the handshake
is 1460 (1448 bytes of data with the Timestamps option). A frame carries 52 bytes of IP, TCP and
option headers more than its data: 1500 bytes of IP for 1448 bytes of data. Observation: level 1, until 1.9 s,
the largest frame of data of host1 has at most 1400 bytes of IP, the route MTU.

%# parameter: Tcp.pathMtu
%# class: route
%# value: 1400
%# key: *.host1.tcp.pathMtu
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpPathMtuRoute")
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                        .filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B")
                                        .captureMax("largest", "ipv4.totalLengthField")
                                        .within(2.0)))
        .act(action().at(1.9)
                 .describe("the largest frame of data until 1.9 s")
                 .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "{largest} <= 1400B"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpPathMtuRoute compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.pathMtu = 1400    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 1000000B
sim-time-limit = 2s
*.host1.tcp.mtuProbing = 2
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpPathMtuRoute: PASS
